            <p>The biggest lever is your factory's minimum order quantity — a factory that requires 1,000+ pieces per style forces you to either overspend on inventory or skip styles you wanted to launch with. Working with a 300-piece MOQ factory lets you launch 2-3 styles instead of one, test colorways, and still keep total production spend under $10,000. Beyond that: use freelancers instead of agencies for branding, start with Shopify Basic instead of a custom build, and hold off on paid ads until organic content proves what actually sells.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
      document.querySelectorAll('.faq__question').forEach(btn => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const isOpen = btn.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
          document.querySelectorAll('.faq__question').forEach(b => {
            b.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
            b.nextElementSibling?.classList.remove('faq__answer--visible');
          });
          if (!isOpen) {
            btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
            btn.nextElementSibling?.classList.add('faq__answer--visible');
          }
        });
      });
    });
  </script>

